wineserver: keep the security descriptors programs write on files and folders

Wine derives a file's security descriptor from its Unix mode, so an ACL a
program sets reads back different (no inherited flags, no Users or
Administrators entries). The Battle.net Agent sets ACLs on a game folder
before patching, reads them back, and stops with "Unable to fix permissions"
(BLZBNTAGT00000846): Diablo II: Resurrected could not update.

Store the descriptor written in a "user.wine.sd" xattr with the Unix
permission bits it was written for, and return it while those bits are
unchanged. A chmod made from macOS falls back to the mode-derived descriptor.
The xattr is read on every query, so a handle opened before another handle
changed the ACL sees the change too (engine-v1.7).
The Unix mode is still set from the DACL as before.

